# Intent: Encrypted link, step 1 (off by default, CONFIG_MAIPAI_LINK_PSK): X25519 through the crypto service (new key pair, shared secret, key destroyed after use), the 32-byte link key in flash (namespace mp_link), and a bench tool self.bench.link_selftest that runs a whole local exchange with the key schedule of maipai_linkkey_core.h and reports agreement, the time in ms and the dip of free internal RAM. Off: no code, no memory.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: on an image built with the linkpsk overlay self.bench.link_selftest answers agree true and a time and RAM dip; on the default image the tool does not exist.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_LINK_PSK (default n)

